    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7883a8a03fc28901a0449868304d5d&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Admissions Advisor Location: Detroit, MI Job Id: 222 # of Openings: 0 Admissions Advisor Position Summary: The Public Safety Student Admissions Advisor is responsible for recruiting, advising,  and enrolling adult students into Cleary University’s Adult Accelerated programs,  with a primary focus on individuals working in law enforcement, fire, EMS,  corrections, and other public safety-related professions. This is an enrollment-focused admissions position requiring a strong ability to  engage prospective students, build relationships, manage an active recruitment  pipeline, provide consistent follow-up, and guide individuals through the admissions  and enrollment process. The Advisor is expected to contribute directly to established  enrollment goals while taking ownership of prospective students from initial inquiry  through enrollment and successful start. The Advisor actively engages prospective students through proactive phone  outreach, text, email, virtual meetings, onsite Public Safety events, agency visits, and  community-based outreach. This position requires demonstrated experience in  recruitment, admissions, relationship development, sales, or a similarly goal oriented environment, along with strong communication skills, comfort working  toward measurable enrollment outcomes, proficiency with technology (Salesforce, ZoomInfo, Microsoft Teams), and the ability to build credibility and relationships  with working adults and Public Safety professionals. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Recruit and enroll Adult Accelerated and Public Safety students through  proactive outreach, relationship-based recruitment, personalized advising,  and consistent follow-up using Salesforce, ZoomInfo, Microsoft Teams, and  multiple communication channels. Manage and advance an active admissions pipeline by developing  relationships with prospective students, understanding their educational and  career goals, addressing questions and potential barriers, and guiding  students from inquiry through application, enrollment, registration, and start. Meet established enrollment and recruitment activity goals while delivering a  highly supportive, student-centered admissions experience tailored to  working adults and Public Safety professionals. Primary Responsibilities • Develop and implement recruitment strategies to increase inquiries,  applications, enrollments, and starts among Adult Accelerated and Public  Safety student populations. • Conduct consistent and proactive outreach through phone, text, email,  Salesforce, ZoomInfo, virtual meetings, and in-person appointments. • Take ownership of assigned prospective students from initial inquiry through  successful enrollment and start. • Use a relationship-based recruitment approach to understand prospective  students' professional goals, educational needs, concerns, and decision making factors. • Clearly communicate Cleary University's academic programs and the benefits  of accelerated education for working adults and Public Safety professionals. • Effectively address questions and concerns related to cost, time, transfer  credit, work schedules, tuition reimbursement, and returning to school. • Clearly communicate next steps, requirements, and deadlines to help  prospective students progress through the enrollment process. • Maintain consistent and professional follow-up throughout the admissions  cycle. • Re-engage inactive leads, incomplete applicants, previous inquiries, and other  prospective student populations to identify additional enrollment  opportunities. • Lead presentations, information sessions, and 1:1 advising appointments  tailored to adult learners and Public Safety professionals. • Represent Cleary University at police departments, fire departments,  correctional facilities, Public Safety agencies, employer sites, community  organizations, and recruitment events. • Collaborate with Enrollment Leadership to identify admissions barriers and  recommend solutions to improve the prospective student experience and  enrollment outcomes. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor's degree required. • Demonstrated experience in admissions, recruitment, sales, business  development, outreach, or another goal-oriented, relationship-based  environment. • Demonstrated ability to proactively engage prospective students or  customers, build relationships, manage a pipeline, provide consistent follow up, and achieve established goals. • Strong telephone, interpersonal, and relationship-development skills. • Experience working toward measurable enrollment, recruitment, sales, or  production goals. • Proficiency with CRM systems (Salesforce strongly preferred), ZoomInfo, and  Microsoft Teams. • Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage  working adults and Public Safety professionals. • Highly organized with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage  multiple priorities and a large prospective student pipeline. • Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, goal oriented and results-driven environment. • Availability for evening, weekend, and regional travel. Preferred Qualifications: • Three or more years of successful experience in admissions, recruitment,  sales, business development, or a similarly goal-oriented field. • Experience in higher education admissions with demonstrated success  meeting or exceeding enrollment goals. • Experience working with non-traditional, adult, or accelerated student  populations. • Experience working with law enforcement, fire, EMS, corrections, government,  or other Public Safety populations. • Background in employer partnerships, business development, or workforce  development initiatives. • Understanding of adult learning needs, Prior Learning Assessment, transfer  credit, tuition reimbursement, and accelerated degree-completion pathways. Key Attributes and Competencies: • Strong recruitment orientation with a demonstrated drive to achieve  enrollment goals. • Proactive and persistent in prospective student outreach and follow-up. • Ability to build rapport quickly, understand prospective student needs,  address concerns, and encourage appropriate next steps. • Strong relationship-building abilities with prospective students, internal  teams, and external Public Safety partners. • Comfortable working with performance metrics and being accountable for  individual enrollment results. • Self-motivated, resilient, and results-oriented. • Creative, solutions-oriented, and adaptable in a fast-paced environment. • Ability to analyze data, prioritize outreach, manage a pipeline, and meet  enrollment goals. • Student-centered approach combined with a strong focus on enrollment  outcomes. • Commitment to continuous improvement and professional growth. • Positive attitude and strong team orientation aligned with Cleary University's  mission and values. Physical Demands and Working Conditions: • Ability to lift up to 10 pounds. • Regularly required to speak, listen, sit, and use technology for extended  periods. • Onsite work required including occasional evening and weekend work. • Local and regional travel to employer sites, community organizations, and  recruitment events. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all  backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race,  color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability,  veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89f8b940c019fc96881a67f80&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker: Admissions Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 216 # of Openings: 0 Student Worker: Clerical Assistant General Description The team of student workers provides support to run the daily operations of the Admissions Office. The primary way in which they offer support is by providing event support when guests attend recruitment events on campus. The student worker also provides secondary support to the main Admissions Office where guests check in for their campus visits. Lastly, student workers occasionally provide support by entering all prospective student data into the campus database for Admissions Staff to use during the recruitment process. Specific Responsibilities 85% Event and Campus Visit Support Greet and register visitors, and issue any required identification badges, parking information, and visit schedule. Prepare for tours by putting together tour items such as draw string bags, and program folders. Escort individuals or groups around campus, on campus tours, or through places of interest. Provide directions and other pertinent information to visitors. Distribute brochures, program information, and explain admission and registration processes and operations. Support admissions office with on-campus events. Be service orientated by actively looking for ways to help staff and visitors. Operate campus telephone line to answer, screen, or forward calls, this includes: providing information, taking messages, or scheduling appointments. 10% Front Office Support Greet visitors entering the office, determine nature and purpose of visit, and direct or escort the visitors to specific destinations. Provide information about establishment, such as location of departments or offices, employees within the organization, or services provided. Collect, sort, distribute, or prepare mail, messages, or courier deliveries. Maintain storage areas Perform the process of opening and closing the office when needed 5% Data Entry Receive, verify, and process all pieces of the application file, including but not limited to the application for admission, character recommendation, high school transcript, college transcript, and ACT/SAT score in database. Receive, verify, and process all prospective student inquires. Enter prospective student data from info cards obtained through various on and off campus events. Load batch lists into database. Execute all of Admissions data entry, daily and event based recruitment mailings, and daily recruitment correspondence including daily tracker actions. Create/edit all student records in the database for both candidates and applicants, ensuring complete biographical and mailing data in each student record. Present completed applicant files to the Admissions Counselor for review and acceptance Receive, verify, and process all pieces submitted by accepted applicants, including but not limited to the immunization forms and final high school transcripts At all times and in all situations, represent CU and the Admissions Department in a professional and friendly manner Minimum Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent is required. Experience in an office setting preferred. Must be a current student at Cleary University and be in good standing with the university. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to relate well with different people in a variety of situations Excellent communication skills Ability to communicate effectively with other offices on campus Thoroughly understands the admissions strategy and procedures Ability to use computers and basic programs (campus database, e-mail, Microsoft Office, internet etc.) Ability to be self-motivated and self-managed to meet deadlines Ability to plan and execute duties with attention to detail Ability to problem-solve and make reasoned decisions Be able to meet deadlines, be flexible, and most of all be team-oriented Knowledgeable about basic university policies in the areas of housing, financial aid, parking, and academic programs Ability to work independently and adapt to a variety of roles and environments Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with multiple demands Ability to work with a team of admissions personnel in an office setting Have critical thinking ability by using logic and reasoning to identify the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions, conclusions or approaches to problems. Providing information to supervisors, co-workers, and other admissions staff by telephone, in written form, email, or in person. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a19fd3ba9001a011540d644350&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Assistant Baseball Coach Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 219 # of Openings: 0 ASSISTANT BASEBALL COACH JOB SUMMARY: The Assistant Baseball Coach will support the daily operations of the Cleary University Baseball program. The Assistant Baseball Coach will aid the Head Coach in team management, training, recruitment, and academic oversight, while contributing to the success and integrity of Cleary's NAIA athletics. JOB DUTIES : Assist in planning and conducting practices, workouts, and competitions. Support the Head Coach in implementing strategic game plans and performance improvement. Aid in the identification and recruitment of prospective student-athletes who align with Cleary’s academic and athletic standards. Promote and monitor the academic success of student-athletes, encouraging use of Cleary support resources (e.g., study tables, tutoring). Help coordinate team travel, logistics, and equipment management. Represent Cleary Athletics in a professional and sportsmanlike manner on and off the field. Engage in departmental fundraising, community outreach, and athletic promotional activities. Ensure compliance with NAIA, WHAC Conference, and Cleary University rules and policies. Serve as a positive mentor, modeling integrity, accountability, and leadership. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Prior coaching experience at the collegiate, club, or high school level preferred. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work flexible hours including evenings, weekends, and travel. CPR/AED certification or willingness to obtain upon hiring. Valid driver’s license and ability to be cleared to drive university vehicles. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
