    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7885a89e235a1d019e40590a9c158c&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Sports Information Graduate Assistant Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 196 # of Openings: 0 SPORTS INFORMATION GRADUATE ASSISTANT JOB SUMMARY: The Athletic Department Graduate Assistant will assist the athletic department administration with the daily operational tasks.  The Graduate Assistant will be involved in every aspect of the athletic department, including, but not limited to, compliance, facility management, sports information, marketing, game operations, business aspects and other areas assigned by the athletic administration. JOB DUTIES: Responsible for assisting in the planning, directing, and evaluating all aspects and facets of a successful program at the NAIA level. Aiding the Sports Information Director with taking stats, preparing news releases and feature articles for the Cougars Website, and documenting special athletic events. Facilitating athletic department community service and fundraising events. Providing support to all coaches when necessary. Oversee administrative processes and procedures as assigned. Serve as a leader, mentor, and role-model to the student-athletes of the athletic department. Contribute to maintaining the Athletic Department website and social media platforms, along with marketing of the Cleary University Athletic Department. Ensure accurate stats at assigned home contests and oversee quick delivery of stats to opposing teams. Ensure excellent, timely, and accurate information on electronic and printed material that pertains to the athletic department. Write and edit game summaries for some athletic events. Provide game updates and promote Cleary University through various social media platforms. Any other duties assigned by the Athletic Administration. QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required and be accepted into the Cleary University graduate program. Candidate must be enrolled in at least one graduate class per session (three credits) and remain in good academic standing (3.0 or higher GPA). The Graduate Assistant will receive a 75% graduate tuition scholarship provided the above standard and requirements are met. Previous experience as a student-athlete or employment within a collegiate athletic department. Ability to frequently work weekends and nights, totaling 15-20 hours a week. Strong organizational skills with an ability to effectively multi-task are essential. Excellent oral and written communication skills, computer literacy and strong interpersonal skills to work with various college constituencies. The ability to work a flexible and irregular schedule. Works well as a team member or independently. Excels in prioritizing multiple tasks with attention to detail, problem solving and follow-through to consistently meet expectations and deadlines. Ability to work with students and diverse constituencies. A positive attitude and an understanding of the importance of being open-minded and flexible. Travel is necessary with a valid driver’s license required. Ability to successfully pass a background check also required. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a7887a89d02e588019d4a9613590f29&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Chief Financial Officer Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 182 # of Openings: 0 Chief Financial Officer Howell, Michigan  |  Full-Time | Exempt Cleary University seeks a strategic and entrepreneurial Chief Financial Officer (CFO) to guide the financial strategy of a growing and rapidly evolving private university based in Howell, Michigan. In recent years, Cleary has strengthened its financial foundation, doubled enrollment, and developed a distinctive reputation for accelerated degree pathways serving working adults. These offerings have generated thousands of incremental enrollments with a 78% retention rate and a strong job placement rate, reflecting the strength of Cleary’s workforce-aligned model and its growing regional reputation. Reporting directly to President Alan Drimmer and serving as a key member of the executive leadership team, the CFO will work closely with the President to guide financial strategy, strengthen institutional planning and investments in financial systems, and support the university’s continued growth and innovation. The successful candidate will join a nimble leadership team and help build the financial frameworks needed to support program expansion, national initiatives, and new strategic ventures, while ensuring that financial strategy remains closely aligned with Cleary’s mission of preparing career-ready graduates. Cleary enters this search during a period of continued strategic investment and institutional progress. The University generates approximately $35 million in tuition revenue and is advancing a set of mission-aligned initiatives designed to expand access, improve outcomes, and strengthen its financial position, including: National expansion of Cleary’s accelerated programs in several major metropolitan cities and consideration of a for-profit entity to support growth Development of new schools and academic programs aligned with labor market trends Rollout of an innovative career development pathway model New philanthropy initiatives, including the development of a capital campaign Expansion of campus footprint These initiatives reflect the university’s commitment to disciplined growth and long-term financial strength. In addition, the University has just rolled out its new strategic plan, The Fourth Wave, and the plan presents an exciting opportunity for a CFO to lead financial transformation within a high-growth education model. As the institution scales its nationally expanding adult and online programs—already demonstrating strong revenue generation and retention—while reinvesting in a vibrant residential campus, the CFO will shape a dynamic financial architecture that balances growth, margin, and mission. This role offers the chance to build sophisticated segment-level economics, optimize pricing and discount strategies across diverse student populations, and deploy capital in ways that directly fuel enrollment growth, program innovation, and long-term financial sustainability. The successful candidate will be a collaborative, hands-on financial leader who brings both strategic perspective and strong operational capability. The CFO will serve as a trusted partner to the President and senior leadership team, thrive in a lean and entrepreneurial environment, and share Cleary’s commitment to practical, career-focused education for working adults and diverse student populations. This is an on-site position reporting to the President and units reporting to the CFO include Budget, Accounting, Student Business Office, Payroll, and Facilities. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The Chief Financial Officer oversees all university budgeting, accounting, financial analysis, and financial reporting functions and ensures that the university’s financial statements adhere to generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), working closely with external auditors. The CFO also oversees tax reporting and ensures that university operations comply with Internal Revenue Service (IRS) regulations and applicable State of Michigan requirements. In addition, the CFO develops and implements policies, standards, and procedures related to the university’s financial operations and ensures appropriate legal and regulatory compliance. Candidates for the CFO position will also be expected to: Serve as a strategic partner to the President and executive leadership team in aligning financial planning with institutional priorities, program innovation, and long-term growth initiatives Develop and monitor financial models, analyses, and interpretation of statistical and accounting information to assess operating results Oversee the University’s system of accounts and records on all University transactions and assets Coordinate and direct the preparation of the budget and financial forecasts Establish major financial objectives and policies for the institution and prepare reports that outline the University’s financial position in the areas of income, expenses and earnings based on past, present and future operations Collaborate with advancement leadership to support evolving philanthropic efforts and ensure strong financial infrastructure for future fundraising initiatives KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of university administration and the principles and practices of financial management Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and complex tasks simultaneously Experience with automated accounting systems and financial reporting tools Ability to build effective working relationships with diverse stakeholders across the university Demonstrated leadership ability, including supervising staff, delegating responsibilities, and fostering a collaborative team environment Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain a high level of confidentiality, and uphold institutional policies and priorities Demonstrated ability to connect financial strategy with institutional mission and student outcomes MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in finance, business, accounting, or a related field Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience in accounting or financial management in progressively responsible positions within a higher education institution; Or Five (5) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in financial planning, budgeting, and financial operations PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in finance, business, accounting, or a related field CPA certification About the Institution Cleary University is a private institution founded in 1883 with a long-standing commitment to innovation, applied learning, and entrepreneurship in business education. Located in Howell, Michigan, the University offers associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degree programs designed to prepare students for immediate and sustained success in a rapidly evolving workforce. Cleary’s main campus is in Livingston County, with an additional education center in Detroit that extends its reach into one of the region’s major economic hubs. At the core of the academic experience is The Cleary Mind™, a distinctive, data-informed curricular framework focused on developing eight attributes most valued by employers: critical thinking, problem solving, ethics, creative thinking, communication, persuasion, entrepreneurship, and leadership. Fully integrated across the curriculum and co-curricular experience, The Cleary Mind™ reflects Cleary’s commitment to aligning academic programs with workforce needs and ensuring graduates are prepared to succeed and lead in dynamic organizational environments. Cleary serves a vibrant, career-focused student population, including traditional undergraduates as well as working professionals pursuing hybrid and fully online programs. Traditional undergraduate students may live in university residence halls, off-campus housing, or commute from home. The University’s emphasis on small class sizes, personalized support, and strong industry alignment fosters meaningful student engagement and career readiness. Cleary’s athletic teams, known as the Cougars, are an integral part of campus life, competing at the NAIA level as a member of the Wolverine-Hoosier Athletic Conference. Learn more about Cleary University at www.cleary.edu. Living in the Area Cleary’s main campus is in Howell, Michigan, part of Livingston County, one of the fastest-growing regions in Southeast Michigan. Howell offers a blend of small-town charm and access to major metropolitan opportunities, situated halfway between Detroit and Lansing, within easy driving distance of Ann Arbor, and less than an hour from Detroit Metropolitan Airport, providing convenient regional and national connectivity. The region is known for its highly ranked public schools and family-friendly communities; abundant outdoor recreation, including lakes, parks, and trails; and a revitalized historic downtown featuring restaurants, arts venues, and year-round community events. Residents also benefit from proximity to major employers and innovation hubs across Southeast Michigan. The area offers a high quality of life, combining affordability, safety, and natural beauty with convenient access to the economic, cultural, and educational assets of Michigan’s leading cities. Learn more about the region at www.livgov.com. To Apply To be considered, you must apply directly at: https://acesrch.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a21esjy30qw5 Please apply through the application link and do not email applications. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and should include a cover letter and curriculum vita. Ideally cover letters should not exceed two pages. All applications are treated confidentially. Inquiries, referrals, and nominations are also treated confidentially. Inquiries and questions: Please send to ClearyCFO@acesrch.com Nominations and referrals: Please send the nominee’s name, title, and contact information if available to nominations@acesrch.com Institutional Information Cleary University is committed to being a workplace that is not only free of discrimination, but one that genuinely fosters inclusion and belonging. Cleary strongly believes that workforce diversity creates an environment in which its employees can thrive. Cleary understands and embraces the variety through which people gain experiences whether through professional, personal, educational, or volunteer opportunities. Cleary University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78839fa064212401a0690778775454&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Prep Cook Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 223 # of Openings: 0 Cook SUMMARY OF BASIC JOB FUNCTION: The Cleary University Prep Cook (afternoons/early evening shift) role will involve performing meal-prep activities, ensuring food plating is visually appealing, and maintaining cleanliness in your station. You will also work as a team with others to ensure a clean and quality buffet. Replace low or empty containers on the buffet with clean containers full of fresh products. Serve food at proper temperatures. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: You must be at least 18 years of age to be considered for this role. Proven ability to read and understand recipes. Demonstrates passion and enthusiasm for working in the kitchen. Actively represents the Cleary University to students. Proven knowledge of culinary techniques and terminology Demonstrates excellent guest service skills and an ability to give appropriate service recovery. NON-ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Actively participates in meetings. Supervised by : Director of Hospitality & Food Service Education/Experience : High School Diploma; experience in prep and service. Language Ability: Ability to read and interpret documents such as manuals and write routine reports.  Ability to apply common sense understanding to carry out instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form, ability to speak effectively before groups of customers or employees of organization. Physical Demands and Work Environment: The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include ability to adjust focus. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; use hands to finger, handle, or feel and talk and/or hear. The employee is frequently required to walk and reach with hands and arms. The employee is occasionally required to sit.  The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate to high. Regular and predictable attendance is required. Cleary University is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78839f9fd3ba8701a033aeb2456c13&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker - Clancy's Cashier Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 220 # of Openings: 0 Clancy's Student Worker Cashier JOB SUMMARY: The Student Employee will support the daily operations of the Clancy's Café. This role provides hands-on experience in hospitality & food service while promoting a positive environment for Cleary University Clancy's team. The cashier will scan meal cards into the point-of-sale system from students who have purchased the meal plan to record their visit. The cashier will also ring up all non-meal plan customers using the Squares terminal. There are no cash handling responsibilities since all transactions are by credit card or house account. Cashier's are eligible to receive one complimentary meal per shift. Available shifts are: Breakfast= 8am-9:30am Lunch= 11:30am-1:30pm Dinner 5pm-7pm Saturday Brunch= 11am-1pm QUALIFICATIONS: Current Cleary University in good academic standing Interest in business administration, finance,  corporate accounting or related fields Excellent communication and teamwork skills Ability to work evenings, weekends, and flexible hours based on event schedules Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d096d0d55a019731393c7f56d9&id=8a78859e9fd3bb25019fd7e3f4b414e7&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Cleary University",
      "description": "Cleary University Home Position: Student Worker: Museum Assistant Location: Howell, MI Job Id: 217 # of Openings: 0 Museum Assistant: Arthur Secunda Museum Duties Under the direction of the Curator, the Museum Assistant will work on museum collections and programs: Collections Conduct collections inventory, checking work against collections management system (CMS) database Update object locations in CMS Assist with artifact handling, moving, and hanging Insert acid-free tissue as interleaving in flat file drawers Assist with cataloguing Cleary history material Rehouse Arthur Secunda and Cleary history archival material in acid-free folders and boxes Develop inventories of archival material Dismantle Cleary history shadowboxes to preserve historic documents Programs Assist with museum programs by facilitating art activities and giving museum information at events such including Secunda Second Sunday, High School Immersive Experience, Cleary Days, Night at the Museum, and offsite partner events Develop programs and program activities as needed Complete other duties as assigned related to museum exhibits and other projects Skills Artifact handling Museum registration and collections management basics Museum education best practices Program and event development Nonprofit cultural organization administration basics Requirements Must be a Cleary University Student Must be available to work at Secunda Museum events Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by Cleary University"
    }
